urces Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Admissions Ambassador – H. Howell [work study] Admissions Ambassador – H. Howell [work study] Work-Study (AULA) Los Angeles, CA Posted 1 month ago Antioch University Los Angeles Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 3 Hours per Week: 20 hrs/wk per position Weekends Required: There may be times when asked to cover weekend events. Evenings Required: There may be times when asked to cover weekend events. Supervisor: Heather Howell Alternate Supervisor: Ozzie Rodriguez This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 50% - Reports, Assist Zoom Room Front Desk, Processing Documents, Emails, projects Method to assess remote work: Report Dashboards, Daily Zoom Check-ins, Google Chat Check-in/out Job Description 10 hours Assist the Office of Admissions with assembling information packets, preparing admissions materials and mailings. Assist at the welcome desk. Assist with inventory management of admissions collateral materials. Data entry of new prospects and applications. Process admission materials. Answer Admissions general phone line and emails. Assist with Campus Tours 2-4 hours Assist with events. 1-2 hours Provide campus tours for prospective students 2 hours Serve as a student panelist at admissions events. 2 hours Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Must be Federal Work-Study (FWS) eligible through your institution. Reliable availability of up to 20 hours weekdays between the hours of 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM PT (Flexible schedule) Able to commute to Campus for 1 or more weekdays per week Ability to work independently Strong organization and follow-through Clear, warm written communication Comfortable on phones and speaking to students Comfortable with Zoom, Google Workspace/Drive; willing to learn Collaborative, community-minded, and able to hold confidentiality Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? I am not sure How to Apply: Please email your resume to Kelly Oakley, Enrollment & Events Coordinator Email: koakley@antioch.edu (Different from Supervisor) Position Type: Work Study Department: Admissions To apply for this job email your details to koakley@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Previous Slide Next Slide Share Facebook Twitter Linkedin Pinterest Email Instagram Hide photo (admin) Add ID to the Hide Specific Photos setting:"
