nects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Dept. Asst. - Doctoral Research Fellow - J. Bergkamp [Work Study] Dept. Asst. - Doctoral Research Fellow - J. Bergkamp [Work Study] Work-Study (AUS) Seattle, WA Posted 3 months ago Antioch University Seattle * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 10/1/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 4; Similar from many years past, fellows are assigned to support faculty-led research labs and teaching. Considering that we have approximately 8 faculty, 4 fellows are needed. Hours per Week: 15 a week Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Jude Bergkamp Alternate Supervisor: Melissa Kennedy This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 50-75% Method to assess remote work: Weekly meetings with the supervisor, project management tracking tasks. Job Description The Doctoral Research Fellows engaging and assistant teaching, research, and program development throughout the year. Hours depend on faculty assignments and specific evolving tasks. Qualifications An AUS PsyD student in good standing in 