      "title": "Teaching Asst. -Conservation Biology",
      "description": "Teaching Asst. -Conservation Biology - M. Akresh [Work Study] - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Teaching Asst. -Conservation Biology - M. Akresh [Work Study] Teaching Asst. -Conservation Biology - M. Akresh [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Keene, NH Posted 3 months ago Antioch Univesity New England * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 8/31/2026 End Date: 12/12/2026 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: 10 Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Michael Akresh Alternate Supervisor: Rachel Thiet This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 25%, see below. Method to assess remote work: Supervisor will be in weekly communication with the student to monitor that the work is being completed. Supervisor will track completed tasks. See below for outcomes. Job Description Teaching Assistant for Conservation Biology class (ESS 5630) in the fall. Attend class sessions (fully in person) and help answer questions and provide support to small groups of students during in-class labs (3.5 hours/week). Arrange time outside of class to be available to students for working on class assignments and the final project, and to provide tutoring in content and skills to students who need additional support (3 hours/week). Assistant may also help with grading assignments (1.5 hour/week), finding Conservation Biology topics in the current news (1 hour/week), and preparing for class (1 hour/week). Work will occur during class time as well as outside of class as arranged with individuals or groups of students. Qualifications Applicants should have: A strong background in Conservation Biology, and have already taken the class at AUNE in a past year. Strong communication skills and attention to detail Ability and interest in working with other graduate students to build knowledge and skills Ability to attend class on Fridays Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Please send a brief cover letter and your CV. Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: ES To apply for this job email your details to makresh@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.antioch.edu/job/research-assistant-aune-psyd/": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Research Assistant - AUNE PsyD - K. Russell [Work Study] - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Research Assistant - AUNE PsyD - K. Russell [Work Study] Research Assistant - AUNE PsyD - K. Russell [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Remote (Remote) Posted 3 months ago Antioch University New England * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 9/1/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 1-2 (hours can be divided among two students) Hours per Week: 4 hours per week for 2 students or 8 hours per week for 1 student Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Katherine Russell Alternate Supervisor: Becca Stackpole This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 100% This is a remote position that will involve literature searches and preparation of research proposals, as well as virtual research meetings. Method to assess remote work: Student will check in regularly with the supervisor about their progress and submit work. This work will hopefully lead to the development of a research proposal and/or conference presentation. Job Description The student will assist with research development and preparation of a research proposal. This will include review of relevant literature, remote meetings, and writing. Research topics include: (a) integrative psychotherapy and therapeutic practices, and (b) non-death, intangible losses and grief. Qualifications Must be a doctoral student in good academic standing; prior research experience a plus Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Email a CV and a letter of interest to the supervisor Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: Clinical Psychology, AUNE PsyD To apply for this job email your details to krussell1@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.antioch.edu/job/dept-asst-strategic-partnerships-marketing-and-outreach-j-glover-work-study-6/": {
      "title": "Dept. Asst.",
      "description": "Dept. Asst. - Strategic Partnerships Marketing and Outreach - J. Glover [Work Study] - Antioch University We Value Your Privacy At Antioch University, we value your privacy. Cookies are used to improve the quality of our website and your journey with us. By continuing to browse this website, you agree to the use of these cookies. Privacy Policy OK Customize Consent Preferences We use cookies to help you navigate efficiently and perform certain functions. You will find detailed information about all cookies under each consent category below. The cookies that are categorized as \"Necessary\" are stored on your browser as they are essential for enabling the basic functionalities of the site. ... Show more Necessary Always Active Necessary cookies are required to enable the basic features of this site, such as providing secure log-in or adjusting your consent preferences. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable data. No cookies to display. Functional Functional cookies help perform certain functionalities like sharing the content of the website on social media platforms, collecting feedback, and other third-party features. No cookies to display. Analytics Analytical cookies are used to understand how visitors interact with the website. These cookies help provide information on metrics such as the number of visitors, bounce rate, traffic source, etc. No cookies to display. Performance Performance cookies are used to understand and analyze the key performance indexes of the website which helps in delivering a better user experience for the visitors. No cookies to display. Advertisement Advertisement cookies are used to provide visitors with customized advertisements based on the pages you visited previously and to analyze the effectiveness of the ad campaigns. No cookies to display. Save My Preferences OK Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Dept. Asst. - Strategic Partnerships Marketing and Outreach - J. Glover [Work Study] Dept. Asst. - Strategic Partnerships Marketing and Outreach - J. Glover [Work Study] Work-Study (GSLC) Remote (Remote) Posted 3 months ago Antioch University GSLC * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 8/17/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: 10 hrs/1 student Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Jessie Glover Alternate Supervisor: Michelle Koppitz This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 100% of work will be remote. Some virtual meetings will be required. Method to assess remote work: Job Description Position Summary The office of Strategic Initiatives seeks a Marketing and outreach Assistant to support its efforts building workforce development and education opportunities in partnership with employer and member organizations in a wide range of industries. This work is supported by Antioch University and the Coalition for the Common Good.The Strategic Partnerships Marketing & Outreach Assistant supports the team's communication and engagement efforts by preparing marketing assets, maintaining digital communications, and promoting partnership initiatives. Working from established brand standards and templates, this student employee helps to create professional materials that communicate the impact of the Strategic Partnerships team and support outreach to organizations and prospective learners. Essential Responsibilities: Marketing Asset Production (approximately 4 hours) Prepare branded marketing materials using approved templates for print and digital distribution. Customize flyers, presentations, brochures, one-pagers, social media graphics, email graphics, and event materials. Update existing marketing collateral with current information and branding. Assist with organizing and maintaining the department's library of marketing templates and digital assets. Ensure materials are accurate, visually consistent, and aligned with institutional brand standards. Digital Communications & Outreach (approximately 4 hours) Assist with preparing content for newsletters, email campaigns, and partner communications. Draft and format website updates, event announcements, and promotional content. Collaborate with CCG marketing team social media posts that highlight partnership initiatives, events, and success stories. Support outreach efforts by preparing communication materials for prospective and existing partners. Event Marketing Support (approximately 1 hour) Create promotional materials for partnership events, workshops, networking opportunities, and campus visits. Assist with event registration communications and post-event follow-up messaging. Content & Brand Management (approximately 1 hour) Organize digital files, images, logos, and communication resources. Help maintain consistency across marketing materials and communication channels. Proofread content for grammar, formatting, and accuracy before publication. Assist in collecting stories, testimonials, and partnership highlights that showcase the impact of Strategic Partnerships. Qualifications Strong written communication and proofreading skills. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to work independently while managing multiple deadlines. Comfortable learning new software and digital platforms. Creativity within established brand guidelines. Professional communication skills when interacting with faculty, staff, students, and community partners. Desired Skills (Not Required): Experience using Canva, Adobe Express, Microsoft PowerPoint, or similar design tools. Familiarity with social media platforms and content scheduling tools. Experience creating presentations, flyers, or digital marketing materials. Basic knowledge of photography or photo editing. Interest in marketing, communications, storytelling, or nonprofit outreach. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Cover letter and resume. Email: jglover1@antioch.edu Position Type: Work Study Department: Strategic Initiatives To apply for this job email your details to jglover1@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Previous Slide Next Slide Share Facebook Twitter Linkedin Pinterest Email Instagram Hide photo (admin) Add ID to the Hide Specific Photos setting:"
    },
    "https://www.antioch.edu/job/operations-assistant-strategic-partnerships-j-glover-work-study-5/": {
      "title": "Operations Assistant",
      "description": "Operations Assistant - Strategic Partnerships - J. Glover [Work Study] - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Operations Assistant - Strategic Partnerships - J. Glover [Work Study] Operations Assistant - Strategic Partnerships - J. Glover [Work Study] Work-Study (GSLC) Remote (Remote) Posted 3 months ago Antioch University GSLC * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 8/17/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: 10 hrs/1 student Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Jessie Glover Alternate Supervisor: Michelle Koppitz This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 100% Method to assess remote work: Job Description Position Summary: The Strategic Partnerships Operations Assistant supports the daily operations of the Strategic Partnerships team in building higher education and workforce development opportunities for nonprofit, for-profit, and public-sector organizations. This work is supported by Antioch University and the Coalition for the Common Good. The Assistant will coordinate projects, build partnership data assets, document and assist in improving operational processes, and assist with the planning and execution of partnership events. This position offers the opportunity to gain hands-on experience in project management, CRM administration, organizational operations, event coordination, and relationship management. Essential Responsibilities: Project Coordination (approximately 4 hours) Assist with tracking ongoing partnership initiatives and project timelines. The Assistant will have a portfolio of projects to track. Support project documentation and follow up on action items. Support cross-functional projects involving internal departments and external partners. Prepare regular project updates. CRM Management & Reporting (approximately 2 hours) Compile and organize partnership data from multiple sources. Build and maintain reports and dashboards using spreadsheets, CRM reporting tools, and other data platforms. Assist in tracking partnership outcomes, key performance indicators, and engagement metrics for leadership reports. Events & Partnership Logistics (approximately 1 hour) Coordinate logistical details for partnership on-site events, industry conferences other engagement opportunities. Process Improvement & Operations (approximately 2 hours) Document departmental workflows, standard operating procedures, and recurring processes. Assist in identifying opportunities to improve operational efficiency and streamline administrative processes. Build and maintain outreach asset toolboxes. Administrative Support (approximately 1 hour) Assist with calendar coordination and scheduling. Qualifications Strong organizational skills and exceptional attention to detail. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Comfortable learning new software platforms and technology. Proficiency with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace, particularly Excel or Google Sheets. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with a team. Professionalism and discretion when interacting with faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Curiosity and a willingness to improve systems and processes. Desired Skills (Not Required): Experience using CRM platforms (such as Salesforce, HubSpot, Airtable, or similar systems). Experience with spreadsheets, reporting, or basic data analysis. Familiarity with project management tools (Asana, Monday.com, Trello, Microsoft Planner, etc.). Experience coordinating events or volunteers. Interest in community engagement, partnership development, nonprofit organizations, or higher education administration. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Cover letter and resume requested. Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: Strategic Initiatives To apply for this job email your details to jglover1@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
    },
