      "title": "Operations Assistant",
      "description": "Operations Assistant - Strategic Partnerships - J. Glover [Work Study] - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Operations Assistant - Strategic Partnerships - J. Glover [Work Study] Operations Assistant - Strategic Partnerships - J. Glover [Work Study] Work-Study (AUO) Remote (Remote) Posted 3 months ago Antioch University Online * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 8/17/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: 10 hrs/1 student Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Jessie Glover Alternate Supervisor: Michelle Koppitz This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 100% Method to assess remote work: Job Description Position Summary: The Strategic Partnerships Operations Assistant supports the daily operations of the Strategic Partnerships team in building higher education and workforce development opportunities for nonprofit, for-profit, and public-sector organizations. This work is supported by Antioch University and the Coalition for the Common Good. The Assistant will coordinate projects, build partnership data assets, document and assist in improving operational processes, and assist with the planning and execution of partnership events. This position offers the opportunity to gain hands-on experience in project management, CRM administration, organizational operations, event coordination, and relationship management. Essential Responsibilities: Project Coordination (approximately 4 hours) Assist with tracking ongoing partnership initiatives and project timelines. The Assistant will have a portfolio of projects to track. Support project documentation and follow up on action items. Support cross-functional projects involving internal departments and external partners. Prepare regular project updates. CRM Management & Reporting (approximately 2 hours) Compile and organize partnership data from multiple sources. Build and maintain reports and dashboards using spreadsheets, CRM reporting tools, and other data platforms. Assist in tracking partnership outcomes, key performance indicators, and engagement metrics for leadership reports. Events & Partnership Logistics (approximately 1 hour) Coordinate logistical details for partnership on-site events, industry conferences other engagement opportunities. Process Improvement & Operations (approximately 2 hours) Document departmental workflows, standard operating procedures, and recurring processes. Assist in identifying opportunities to improve operational efficiency and streamline administrative processes. Build and maintain outreach asset toolboxes. Administrative Support (approximately 1 hour) Assist with calendar coordination and scheduling. Qualifications Strong organizational skills and exceptional attention to detail. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Comfortable learning new software platforms and technology. Proficiency with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace, particularly Excel or Google Sheets. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with a team. Professionalism and discretion when interacting with faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Curiosity and a willingness to improve systems and processes. Desired Skills (Not Required): Experience using CRM platforms (such as Salesforce, HubSpot, Airtable, or similar systems). Experience with spreadsheets, reporting, or basic data analysis. Familiarity with project management tools (Asana, Monday.com, Trello, Microsoft Planner, etc.). Experience coordinating events or volunteers. Interest in community engagement, partnership development, nonprofit organizations, or higher education administration. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Cover letter and resume requested. Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: Strategic Initiatives To apply for this job email your details to jglover1@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
    },
