retion when interacting with faculty, staff, students, and external partners. Curiosity and a willingness to improve systems and processes. Desired Skills (Not Required): Experience using CRM platforms (such as Salesforce, HubSpot, Airtable, or similar systems). Experience with spreadsheets, reporting, or basic data analysis. Familiarity with project management tools (Asana, Monday.com, Trello, Microsoft Planner, etc.). Experience coordinating events or volunteers. Interest in community engagement, partnership development, nonprofit organizations, or higher education administration. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Cover letter and resume requested. Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: Strategic Initiatives To apply for this job email your details to jglover1@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
