olicies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Dept. Asst. -LGBTQIA+ Specialty - J. Andersen [Work Study] Dept. Asst. -LGBTQIA+ Specialty - J. Andersen [Work Study] Work-Study (AULA) Los Angeles, CA Posted 4 months ago Antioch University Los Angeles * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: 10 hrs/1 student Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Justin Andersen Alternate Supervisor: Tenika Jackson This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): Approximately 75% of the position will be performed remotely. Remote responsibilities include email communication, coordinating community partnerships and events, attending virtual planning meetings, developing program communications, scheduling, and assisting with event planning and other administrative tasks for the LGBTQIA+ Studies concentration. Method to assess remote work: Work will be assessed through weekly supervision meetings, regular progress updates, and completion of assigned tasks. Expected outcomes include timely communication, successful event coordination, completion of administrative projects, and professional collaboration with students, faculty, and community partners. Job Description Collaborate with faculty advisors and student members to plan bi-weekly meetings, events, and discussions. (1 Hour) Lead and facilitate group meetings, ensuring a safe and welcoming space for all members. Assist in managing communications, including email updates, meeting reminders, and social media outreach. (1 Hour) Develop programming and events that support the professional and personal development of LGBTQIA+ students. (5 Hours) Organize and maintain group resources, including meeting notes, educational materials, and relevant literature. (1 Hour) Serve as a liaison between SPECTRUM and other campus organizations to promote collaboration and engagement. (1 Hour) Work with faculty advisors to identify opportunities for group growth and sustainability. Maintain confidentiality and adhere to professional standards of conduct. (1 Hour) Qualifications Passionate about supporting LGBTQIA+ communities and advocating for inclusivity. Strong organizational, communication, and leadership skills. Ability to manage time effectively and work independently. Familiarity with event planning and coordination is a plus. Previous involvement in student organizations or leadership roles is preferred but not required. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Current rehire. New applicants, if needed, should submit a résumé and a brief statement of interest to the supervisor. Email: jandersen1@antioch.edu Position Type: Work Study Department: Masters of Psychology To apply for this job email your details to jandersen1@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Previous Slide Next Slide Share Facebook Twitter Linkedin Pinterest Email Instagram Hide photo (admin) Add ID to the Hide Specific Photos setting:"
