    "https://www.antioch.edu/job/dept-asst-aula-student-affairs-oiesa-work-study/": {
      "title": "Dept Asst.",
      "description": "Dept Asst. - AULA Student Affairs/OIESA - F. Hernandez [Work Study] - Antioch University We Value Your Privacy At Antioch University, we value your privacy. Cookies are used to improve the quality of our website and your journey with us. By continuing to browse this website, you agree to the use of these cookies. Privacy Policy OK Customize Consent Preferences We use cookies to help you navigate efficiently and perform certain functions. You will find detailed information about all cookies under each consent category below. The cookies that are categorized as \"Necessary\" are stored on your browser as they are essential for enabling the basic functionalities of the site. ... Show more Necessary Always Active Necessary cookies are required to enable the basic features of this site, such as providing secure log-in or adjusting your consent preferences. These cookies do not store any personally identifiable data. No cookies to display. Functional Functional cookies help perform certain functionalities like sharing the content of the website on social media platforms, collecting feedback, and other third-party features. No cookies to display. Analytics Analytical cookies are used to understand how visitors interact with the website. These cookies help provide information on metrics such as the number of visitors, bounce rate, traffic source, etc. No cookies to display. Performance Performance cookies are used to understand and analyze the key performance indexes of the website which helps in delivering a better user experience for the visitors. No cookies to display. Advertisement Advertisement cookies are used to provide visitors with customized advertisements based on the pages you visited previously and to analyze the effectiveness of the ad campaigns. No cookies to display. Save My Preferences OK Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Dept Asst. - AULA Student Affairs/OIESA  - F. Hernandez [Work Study] Dept Asst. - AULA Student Affairs/OIESA  - F. Hernandez [Work Study] Work-Study (AULA) Los Angeles, CA Posted 4 months ago Antioch University Los Angeles * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 4, we require coverage for our Virtual and In-Person Office throughout the week Hours per Week: 20 Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Francis Hernandez Alternate Supervisor: Elizabeth Carson-Murphy This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 50% Method to assess remote work: We do weekly check ins with our team members and will have them sign in on our Virtual Office to confirm their work hours. Job Description The Office of Inclusive Excellence and Student Affairs seeks a dedicated and motivated graduate student to support initiatives aimed at fostering an inclusive and supportive campus environment, with a specialized focus on administrative operations supporting our military or veteran student population and adapting to adult learning trends. This role provides an opportunity to contribute to meaningful projects, manage critical administrative functions, engage with diverse stakeholders, and enhance personal and professional development in higher education administration. Key Responsibilities Administrative Support & Compliance: Assist with administrative work related to institutional compliance and record-keeping. Assist with drafting reports, presentations, and maintaining organized, confidential records of program activities, compliance outcomes, and audits. Provide general office support, manage digital documentation, and streamline remote administrative workflows. Veteran Affairs Administration: Assist in the coordination and tracking of administrative tasks, resources, and outreach efforts dedicated to the veteran student community to ensure an inclusive campus climate. Respond to inquiries from veteran students, faculty, and staff, and provide accurate information about available specialized resources. Bookstore Operations: Perform administrative and clerical tasks related to campus/organizational bookstore operations. Assist with tracking and coordinating the distribution of textbooks, supplies, or materials tailored to the needs of non-traditional students and adult learners. Program Support: Assist in the planning, coordination, and execution of programs, workshops, and events, particularly those celebrating and supporting the military or veteran student population and adult learners. Develop promotional materials, including flyers, newsletters, and social media content, to enhance event outreach. Manage event logistics, such as scheduling, securing virtual or physical venues, and coordinating guest speakers or facilitators. Research and Data Collection: Conduct research on adult learning trends, compliance best practices, and veteran resources to inform office initiatives. Collect and analyze data related to the military or veteran student population, bookstore accessibility, and adult learner belonging on campus (e.g., surveys, focus groups) to identify opportunities for improvement. Communication and Outreach: Maintain and update the office’s website and social media platforms. Qualifications Must be a current graduate student at Antioch University and eligible for work-study funding. Strong commitment to supporting the military or veteran student population and understanding adult learning trends. Strong administrative skills with high attention to detail and organizational workflows. Willingness to learn and unlearn. Excellent organizational and time-management skills. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency in Google Workspace. Preferred: Prior experience working with, or a strong preference for supporting, the veteran or military-connected community. Experience or coursework related to administrative compliance, database management, or communications. Experience in program coordination, academic affairs, or student affairs tailored to adult learning trends. Familiarity with social media platforms and website management tools. Strong research and analytical skills. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Application accepted through email and a resume is required Email: fhernandez1@antioch.edu Position Type: Work Study Department: AULA Student Affairs/OIESA Dept To apply for this job email your details to fhernandez1@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Previous Slide Next Slide Share Facebook Twitter Linkedin Pinterest Email Instagram Hide photo (admin) Add ID to the Hide Specific Photos setting:"
    },
