      "description": "Dept. Assistant - AUS Clinic Front Desk - M. Kennedy [Work Study] - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Dept. Assistant - AUS Clinic Front Desk - M. Kennedy [Work Study] Dept. Assistant - AUS Clinic Front Desk - M. Kennedy [Work Study] Work-Study (AUS) Seattle, WA Posted 4 months ago Antioch University Seattle * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 9/27/2026 Number of Positions: 4 - position staffs the front desk for the AUS Clinic and must cover Clinic's hours of operation, daily Hours per Week: 15-20 hrs/wk needed = 15-20 hrs/1 student or 60-80 hrs/4 students Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: Yes Supervisor: Melissa Kennedy Alternate Supervisor: Saori Den This position allows for remote work Yes/No: No Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): N/A Method to assess remote work: N/A Job Description The Antioch Community Counseling and Psychology Clinic is looking for a work study student to fill a Clinic front desk position starting in the Summer '25 quarter. Training for this position would start as soon as possible. The Clinic staff hours are Monday - Thursday 9:30am - 7pm and Friday 9:30am - 5pm. Shifts are generally 4-5 hours long. Responsibilities include: ● Monitoring the Clinic voicemail and email. ● Calling clients to take payments via phone. ● Answering or referring inquiries to the appropriate staff. ● Intake processing via phone or email of new clients including scheduling appointments. ● Maintaining client accounts by obtaining, recording, and updating personal and financial i nformation. ● Protecting client rights by maintaining the confidentiality of personal and financial information. ● Assisting student therapists with Clinic procedures. ● Other projects as assigned by the Clinic coordinator. Qualifications: ● Prior administrative and customer service experience preferred. ● Familiarity with MS Office and Google sheets. ● Strong communication skills. Qualifications Prior administrative and customer service experience preferred. Familiarity with MS Office and Google sheets. Strong communication skills. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: The students complete an application and a provide reference. Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: Administration/Student Affairs To apply for this job email your details to mkennedy1@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
    },
