icies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Dept. Asst. - Seattle Front Desk - S. Titus [Work Study] Dept. Asst. - Seattle Front Desk - S. Titus [Work Study] Work-Study (AUS) Seattle, WA Posted 4 months ago Antioch University Seattle * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 5 Hours per Week: 100 = 20 each student Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Scott Titus Alternate Supervisor: Sue Byers This position allows for remote work Yes/No: No Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): N/A Method to assess remote work: N/A Job Description Provide assistance to Front Desk Coordinator, Campus, and Administrative & Finance team. Duties include: Covering front office and phones, 10 hrs Stocking supplies, equipment maintenance, and periodic facilities checks, 2 hrs Assist in directing faculty, staff, students, and visitors, 2hrs Ensure security at the University’s main point of entry, 2 hrs Provide support for the Director of Administrative Services and other administrative staff as needed, 2 hrs data entry, 1hr research and development for directors and department needs, 1hr Qualifications Service-oriented attitude toward patrons. Reliable in terms of work hours agreed upon Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Respond to posted add with resume and cover letter Email: stitus@antioch.edu Position Type: Work Study Department: Campus Services To apply for this job email your details to stitus@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Previous Slide Next Slide Share Facebook Twitter Linkedin Pinterest Email Instagram Hide photo (admin) Add ID to the Hide Specific Photos setting:"
