niversity? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Dept Asst. - Latinx Institute Graduate - S. Santos Dietz [Work Study] Dept Asst. - Latinx Institute Graduate - S. Santos Dietz [Work Study] Work-Study (AUS) Remote (Remote) Posted 4 months ago Antioch University Seattle * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 2 openings. We are in need of more support as the institute responsibilities continue to grow. We want to include more social media and website content, in addition to administrative tasks and connection to the institute partners. Hours per Week: 20 hrs/1 student Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Syntia Santos Dietz Alternate Supervisor: Mariela Marin This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 100% of the work will be remote. The work will involve administrative tasks for the Latinx Institute, support in organizing tasks and activities, manage social media and website including creating content. Support work with Institute’s partners. Collaborate with the Latinx team in activities created to achieve the Institute goals and mission such as the annual symposium. Method to assess remote work: Assessment will take place through weekly meetings with supervisor and evidence by work submitted biweekly related to established goals. Outcomes are to celebrate, support, share resources, and amplify voices of Latinx people. Students will submit Weekly logs and monthly reports. Job Description Work with the Institute’s director to establish, promote, and grow the Latinx Mental Health and Social Justice Institute in support of the Latinx community. Tasks include: weekly meetings with supervisor (1 - 2 hours), working meetings with other members of the institute as needed (1-2 hours), social media management, content search and delivery (5 – 10 hours), marketing efforts (5 – 10), and engage or lead institute’s projects/initiatives such as service, community engagement, collaborations, and among others (5 – 15 hours). Support the organization of the annual symposium (5 – 15 hours). If proficient in Spanish, creating content/translations to Spanish of different materials (5 – 20 hours). Qualifications Applicants must have interest and understanding of the Latinx community, and commitment to working for their well-being and related social justice issues that affect the community. We are looking for individuals who are organized, are familiar with various social media outlets, have skills for administrative tasks (eg. Create tables, graphs, Power Points, Canva announcements, etc.) and able to take initiative with meeting the goals of the institute. Experience with organizing events and Spanish skills are preferred. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? I am not sure How to Apply: Send letter of interest and CV Email: sdietz@antioch.edu Position Type: Work Study Department: School of Counseling, Psychology, and Therapy To apply for this job email your details to sdietz@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Previous Slide Next Slide Share Facebook Twitter Linkedin Pinterest Email Instagram Hide photo (admin) Add ID to the Hide Specific Photos setting:"
    },
