e to celebrate, support, share resources, and amplify voices of Latinx people. Students will submit Weekly logs and monthly reports. Job Description Work with the Institute’s director to establish, promote, and grow the Latinx Mental Health and Social Justice Institute in support of the Latinx community. Tasks include: weekly meetings with supervisor (1 - 2 hours), working meetings with other members of the institute as needed (1-2 hours), social media management, content search and delivery (5 – 10 hours), marketing efforts (5 – 10), and engage or lead institute’s projects/initiatives such as service, community engagement, collaborations, and among others (5 – 15 hours). Support the organization of the annual symposium (5 – 15 hours). If proficient in Spanish, creating content/translations to Spanish of different materials (5 – 20 hours). Qualifications Applicants must have interest and understanding of the Latinx community, and commitment to working for their well-being and related social justice issues that affect the community. We are looking for individuals who are organized, are familiar with various social media outlets, have skills for administrative tasks (eg. Create tables, graphs, Power Points, Canva announcements, etc.) and able to take initiative with meeting the goals of the institute. Experience with organizing events and Spanish skills are preferred. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? I am not sure How to Apply: Send letter of interest and CV Email: sdietz@antioch.edu Position Type: Work Study Department: School of Counseling, Psychology, and Therapy To apply for this job email your details to sdietz@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Previous Slide Next Slide Share Facebook Twitter Linkedin Pinterest Email Instagram Hide photo (a