ts & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Mentor. - S. Byers [Work Study] Mentor. - S. Byers [Work Study] Work-Study (AUS) Seattle, WA Posted 4 months ago Antioch University Seattle * Applicants must be enrolled students at Antioch University living in the United States* Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 8 - Peer Mentors serve student who apply for mentoring from the Seattle campus. Hours per Week: 3- 5 hours/wk needed = 3-5 hrs/1 student or 24-40 hrs/8 students Weekends Required: Yes Evenings Required: Yes Supervisor: Sue Byers Alternate Supervisor: Ingrid Ingerson This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 65-70% - Mentoring student mentees that have the option of mentoring remotely or in-person. Method to assess remote work: I meet with the Peer Mentors monthly and engage via email with them a minimum of every two weeks. Job Description 3-5 hours per week meeting with mentee to include preparation and gathering resources and support for mentee; Monthly Peer mentor meetings; Participation in training; Community building event planning Office assistant to the Student Services office Qualifications Minimum of 1 year in degree program at Antioch University Seattle; Student in good academic standing; Service oriented; Previous mentoring experience, desired. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? Yes How to Apply: Students apply to serve as Peer Mentors. Students are required to complete the application and provide a recommendation from a faculty/staff. Email: sbyers@antioch.edu Position Type: Work Study Department: Administration/Student Affairs To apply for this job email your details to sbyers@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Previous Slide Next Slide Share Facebook Twitter Linkedin Pinterest Email Instagram Hide photo (admin) Add ID to the Hide Specific Photos setting:"
