practica (contacts made, groups recruited) are documented and verifiable; ADTA student liaison reports on local chapter and national student subcommittee work Job Description Provides support to the Dance/Movement Therapy (DMT) program through outreach, communication, and coordination of dance/movement‑based activities. Assists faculty with choreography preparation for the One Billion Rising event and helps recruit and organize participants for DMT practica. This position supports program operations and community engagement efforts. Qualifications Federal Work‑Study eligibility required; Enrolled student in the AUNE dance/movement therapy program; Strong communication and organizational skills; Takes initiative, and works collaboratively with diverse groups in an inclusive environment; Professionalism and comfort supporting dance/movement‑based programming is a must. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? Yes How to Apply: Email interest to [email protected] ; CV. Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: Relational Therapy/DMT To apply for this job email your details to tkawano@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
    },
