onnects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Research Assistant: Dance/Movement Therapy - D. Nelson [Work Study] Research Assistant: Dance/Movement Therapy - D. Nelson [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Remote (Remote) Posted 4 months ago Antioch University New England Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: 8 Weekends Required: Flexible Evenings Required: Flexible Supervisor: Darci Nelsen Alternate Supervisor: Tomoyo Kawano This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 100% -Review, track and summarize academic literature -Assist in the development of IRB protocols, as well as submission and management -Transcribe interviews, coding, analysis and/or summary of data -Contribute to research and writing efforts toward publication Method to assess remote work: Regular check-in meetings; completion and submission of IRB; documentation and summaries of various steps of the research process; manuscript edits, submission Job Description Responsibilities and breakdown of hours will vary depending on course of the study (6-8 hours): Gather, review, organize current literature Collect, organize data Data analysis Summarize findings Formulate recommendations Contribute to writing efforts toward dissemination of findings Attend project meetings Qualifications Federal Work-study Eligible Dance/Movement therapy background Effective organization, time-management, and communication skills Strong research, analytical, critical thinking, and writing skills Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? Yes How to Apply: CV and cover letter Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: DMT / Relational Therapy To apply for this job email your details to dnelsen@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
    },
