ns Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Dept. Asst. - Front Desk Receptionist/Student Services - C. Lower [Work Study] Dept. Asst. - Front Desk Receptionist/Student Services - C. Lower [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Keene, NH Posted 5 months ago Antioch Unversity New England Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 3 to cover the number of hours needed Hours per Week: 10 - 20 hrs per week/3 students Weekends Required: possible if student is interested and available Evenings Required: possible if student is interested and available Supervisor: Cheryl Lower Alternate Supervisor: Deb Barrett This position allows for remote work Yes/No: No Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): N/A Method to assess remote work: N/A Job Description The person(s) who fill this position will be responsible for: Front Desk: Providing students, employees, visitors and callers with a welcome and attentive presence Checking in and connecting visitors to a campus rep Assisting visitors with navigation Fielding and/or redirecting calls and inquiries as appropriate. Learning and applying emergency protocol Providing administrative task and research support Coordinating deliveries and assisting with mail distribution Student Services: Student success support including data entry Assisting with research Answer basic questions regarding all Student Service Departments Assist with updating student services website and link verification Qualifications A friendly, can-do attitude and outgoing presence with service orientation to reach out and assist others Ability to work with minimal direction;take the initiative to update materials, keep the reception desk tidy, and other tasks as appropriate; and maintain flexibility An energetic and service-minded individual able to organize and truncate assignments to fit work schedule Proven ability to adhere to task and confidentiality requirements Strong attention to detail Ability to respond calmly and quickly in case of an emergency, or in the case of an urgent service request, respond as needed Routine administrative tasks range from stuffing envelopes, helping to create flyers and so forth Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Email Cheryl Lower clower@antioch.edu with resume and cover letter and include hours available to work Email: clower@antioch.edu Position Type: Work Study Department: Campus Admin & Student Services To apply for this job email your details to clower@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Previous Slide Next Slide Share Facebook Twitter Linkedin Pinterest Email Instagram Hide photo (admin) Add ID to the Hide Specific Photos setting:"
