    "https://www.antioch.edu/job/environmental-studies-program-assistant-s-green-work-study/": {
      "title": "Environmental Studies Program Assistant",
      "description": "Environmental Studies Program Assistant - S. Green [Work Study] - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Environmental Studies Program Assistant - S. Green [Work Study] Environmental Studies Program Assistant - S. Green [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Remote (Remote) Posted 5 months ago Antioch Unversity New England Start Date: 8/31/2026 End Date: 5/1/2027 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: 10 hours/week Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Suzanne Green Alternate Supervisor: Amy Roy This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 100% Method to assess remote work: Weekly Zoom meetings with supervisor to assess progress. Development of materials to be included in departmental publications. Also involved with data entry, online research, development of materials to support ES student engagement, and developing work product for social media. Job Description Assisting with the maintenance and updating of student employment and internship resource materials. Creating and developing written, visual, and multimedia content for departmental communications, publications, and social media platforms. Collaborating with the team to develop and maintain the ES Department social media calendar, schedule posts related to departmental events and initiatives, and recommend new content topics. Working independently to gather information, conduct interviews, write and edit content, and design articles for departmental publications. Assist in maintaining a variety of databases utilized by the department for programming Hourly breakdown: 10 hrs/week: 3 hours support for student resource development; 3 hours development of creative content for departmental social media and publications; 3 hours online research for special projects, 1 hr./week supervisory meeting Qualifications Familiarity with Google Workspace or Microsoft Office applications for communication, document preparation, and collaboration. Familiarity with social media platforms such as Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn. • Strong writing, editing, and proofreading skills with attention to detail and accuracy. Graphic design skills, including the ability to utilize platforms such as Canva to create engaging posts and visual content. Strong organizational and time-management skills Ability to work independently and follow through on assignments Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Please submit resume and cover letter to Suzanne Green Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: Environmental Studies To apply for this job email your details to sgreen5@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.antioch.edu/job/place-based-project-assistant-p-bocko-work-study-2/": {
      "title": "Place-based Project Assistant",
      "description": "Place-based Project Assistant - P. Bocko [Work Study] - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Place-based Project Assistant - P. Bocko [Work Study] Place-based Project Assistant - P. Bocko [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Keene, NH Posted 5 months ago Antioch Unviversity New England Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 8/22/2026 Number of Positions: One Hours per Week: 15 hrs / week Weekends Required: Rarely Evenings Required: Rarely Supervisor: Paul Bocko Alternate Supervisor: Carol Renzelman This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 50% Method to assess remote work: Weekly team meetings to discuss progress on tasks and discuss next steps. Job Description The Place-based Education Assistant will assist in the planning and implementation of education programming for the Horatio Colony Nature Preserve. Duties include planning & coordinating public programs (6 hrs.) and developing & leading learning experiences with local citizens, teachers, and students (6 hrs.). In addition, the education assistant will work on a team of one faculty and fellow students to do trail work, boundary marking, upkeep of a cabin, monitoring and maintenance of interpretive trail, and upkeep of signage (3 hrs.). Qualifications Experience in education is always a plus. Trail work and land management experience is helpful. However, this is a job for sharing skills and learning more. Willingness to learn is the most important qualification. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? Yes How to Apply: Submit cover letter and resume to supervisor. Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: Education To apply for this job email your details to pbocko@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.antioch.edu/job/preserve-and-park-research-assistant-p-bocko-work-study/": {
      "title": "Preserve and Park Research Assistant",
      "description": "Preserve and Park Research Assistant - P. Bocko [Work Study] - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Preserve and Park Research Assistant - P. Bocko [Work Study] Preserve and Park Research Assistant - P. Bocko [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Keene, NH Posted 5 months ago Antioch University New England Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 8/22/2026 Number of Positions: One Hours per Week: 15 hrs / wk Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Paul Bocko Alternate Supervisor: Carol Renzelman This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 50% Method to assess remote work: Staff meetings every other week, monitoring the nature preserve and implementation of a park research project are the outcomes. Job Description The assistant will, in part, support management of the Horatio Colony Nature Preserve. Preserve duties include upkeep of cabin (2 hours) and upkeep of signage and supplies at the trailhead kiosk (2 hours). The most significant part of the position is the design, implementation, analysis, and documentation of a field research project at the Ashuelot River Park with a focus on collecting data to inform the possible removal or repair of a dam in the Ashuelot River (11 hours). Possibility for continuation into additional terms. Qualifications Land management and field research experience is a plus. Experience in education is helpful. However, this is a job for sharing skills and learning more. Willingness to learn is the most important qualification. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? Yes How to Apply: Submit cover letter and resume to supervisor. Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: Education Department - Horatio Colony Nature Preserve To apply for this job email your details to pbocko@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
