or Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Environmental Educator - P. Palmiotto [Work Study] Environmental Educator - P. Palmiotto [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Keene, NH Posted 5 months ago Antioch University New England Start Date: 8/31/2026 End Date: 4/30/2027 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: 10 Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Peter Palmiotto Alternate Supervisor: Amy Roy This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 20%. Developing Environmental Educational interpretative materials for Glover Ledge. Method to assess remote work: Bi monthly meetings, review of material created Job Description Development and creation of interpretive signage to be place along barrier-free trail, kiosk and other locations at Glover's Ledge. The goals for the signage are to increase visitor engagement with and connection to the landscape, educate about land use past and present, and to serve as a point of connection between Glover’s Ledge and the surrounding community. The new staff member will pick up where a previous staff member left off and continue to design the wording and images for the signage, add additional signage as needed, and construct and install the signs at Glover’s Ledge. As well as supporting and promoting educational programming on the property, maintaining and enhancing the Glover's Ledge web page and connecting with local schools. Qualifications Qualified applicants will be self-directed individuals with experience with interpretive environmental education or a strong desire to learn by doing. Addition qualifications include: ● Project and time management ● Creativity and design skills ● Artistic skills, drawing and sketching skills desired ● Inclusive storytelling ● Clear verbal and written communication ● Collaboration Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? v How to Apply: Send letter of interest discussing how the position will serve your academic and career goals. Include a resume' Email: ppalmiotto@antioch.edu Position Type: Work Study Department: Environmental Studies To apply for this job email your details to ppalmiotto@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Previous Slide Next Slide Share Facebook Twitter Linkedin Pinterest Email Instagram Hide photo (admin) Add ID to the Hide Specific Photos setting:"
    },
    "https://www.antioch.edu/job/lab-and-herbarium-coordinator-p-palmiotto-work-study/": {
      "title": "Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Project Coordinator - Lab and Herbarium - P. Palmiotto [Work Study] - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Project Coordinator - Lab and Herbarium - P. Palmiotto [Work Study] Project Coordinator - Lab and Herbarium - P. Palmiotto [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Keene, NH Posted 5 months ago Antioch University New England Start Date: 7/6/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: 10 Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Peter Palmiotto Alternate Supervisor: Mike Akresh This position allows for remote work Yes/No: No Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 0% Method to assess remote work: N/A Job Description 1. Environmental Field and Lab Equipment and Instrumentation Purchase, maintain, repair and replace environmental and scientific equipment and instrumentation as needed. Track and record all expenditures related to equipment and instrumentation. Maintain accurate inventory of equipment and instrumentation for internal and student/faculty reference. Coordinate equipment and instrumentation loans among all faculty and students Train students in effective and safe use of all equipment and instrumentation. Update all apps, software, operating systems and firmware as needed. Produce and update guides to lab, herbarium, and equipment and instrumentation use if needed. Develop and maintain Lab and Herbarium Home Page and Equipment Guide using LibGuides platform. Implement regular equipment maintenance program, such as recharging batteries, replacing out-of-date reagents and testing equipment function 2. Herbarium (on campus) The Herbarium at AUNE is housed within the Environmental Studies Department on the Antioch New England campus in Keene, NH. The Herbarium contains over 3000 plant specimens representing about 1000 species, primarily from the New England region, and about 600 mushroom specimens. Environmental Studies faculty and students have been contributing specimens to the herbarium since 1976. Maintain and repair plant, fungi, and lichen specimen collections. Assess collection status and maintain proper filing of specimens by family and species. Regularly update specimen names according to current taxonomic standards. 3. Additional Lab Management Responsibilities Provide appropriate storage, handling and disposal of hazardous chemicals. Assure that the Lab and Herbarium work spaces are clean, safe, and compliant with state and federal safety regulations. Perform other duties, other activities as assigned by supervisor (the ES Administrative Director). Qualifications Exceptional organizational skills, high attention to detail, desire to engage with faculty and students in service role. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Send letter of interest and resume Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: Environmental Studies To apply for this job email your details to ppalmiotto@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
    },
