ry Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Project Asst. -Summit Steward-MERE - P. Palmiotto [Work Study] Project Asst. -Summit Steward-MERE - P. Palmiotto [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Keene, NH Posted 5 months ago Antioch University New England Start Date: 7/6/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: 10 Weekends Required: Yes Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Peter Palmiotto Alternate Supervisor: Amy Roy This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 20 Method to assess remote work: Biweekly check ins, review of project completion, count of contacts made Job Description The student in this position will conduct stewardship duties on Mt. Monadnock during weekend days or other high use days through the year (10hr/wk). Duties include in person discussion with hikers on topics such as hiker preparedness, safety, Leave no trace principles, ecology and history of the mountain as well as the fragility of the summit vegetation (8 hr /wk). The MERE summit stewardship program is part of a regional network of alpine stewards with a mission to conserve the alpine habitat in northeastern north America. Formal programing at visitor center or on the trail or summit could be offered. Web site updates, environmental education material creation, writing of technical bulletin and info-graphics as well as grant writing could be other duties of the position (2 hr/wk). Qualifications Outgoing, positive individual with strong group dynamic skills who enjoys climbing mountains, talking to people. Has strong desire to learn and share what they have learned about the mountain’s cultural and ecological stories. Strong writer and communicator is desired. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? Yes How to Apply: send letter of interest, how position fits into academic goals and include resume' Email: ppalmiotto@antioch.edu Position Type: Work Study Department: Environmental Studies To apply for this job email your details to ppalmiotto@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Previous Slide Next Slide Share Facebook Twitter Linkedin Pinterest Email Instagram Hide photo (admin) Add ID to the Hide Specific Photos setting:"
    },
