y Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Research Asst. - RPAS Data Collection - E. Allyn [Work Study] Research Asst. - RPAS Data Collection - E. Allyn [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Keene, NH Posted 6 months ago Antioch University New England Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 6 - we need this many student to meet the demands of the position Hours per Week: 18-30 hours/6 students Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Elizabeth Allyn Alternate Supervisor: Vincent Pignatiello, PsyD This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 50% - meetings, scoring of protocols, supplmental work Method to assess remote work: Reviewing numbers and recordings of completed RPAS assessments Job Description Students will be engaged in the administration, recording, and scoring of RPAS protocols for the normative data collection project. This research assistantship position requires 3-5 hours per week, with administration needing to take place in-person at the PSC. Additional meetings, scoring of protocols, and supplemental work can be completed virtually. Qualifications Being available to conduct and code Rorschach protocols under the supervision of Vincent Pignatiello. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? Yes How to Apply: Contact Vincent Pignatiello directly. Email: vpignatiello@antioch.edu Position Type: Work Study Department: Clinical Psychology To apply for this job email your details to vpignatiello@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved. Previous Slide Next Slide Share Facebook Twitter Linkedin Pinterest Email Instagram Hide photo (admin) Add ID to the Hide Specific Photos setting:"
