    "https://www.antioch.edu/job/social-media-assistant-l-thomas-work-study-4/": {
      "title": "Social Media Assistant",
      "description": "Social Media Assistant - L. Thomas [Work Study] - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Social Media Assistant - L. Thomas [Work Study] Social Media Assistant - L. Thomas [Work Study] Work-Study (AUNE) Remote (Remote) Posted 6 months ago Antioch University New England Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 8/15/2026 Number of Positions: 1 Hours per Week: up to 20 Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: No Supervisor: Laura Thomas Alternate Supervisor: Susan Dreyer Leon This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 100% Use Canva to generate, curate, and post content across multiple Education Department Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn feeds using Buffer. Method to assess remote work: Weekly reports from Buffer, monitoring of feeds and Buffer Job Description The Social Media & Virtual Events Assistant will support the Continuing Education team by helping manage social media content and providing virtual event support. About 60% of the role will focus on drafting and scheduling posts for the Continuing Education Facebook and LinkedIn pages. The remaining 40% of the role will involve assisting with live Zoom events, including providing technical support, introducing presenters, monitoring the chat, and ensuring smooth event delivery. Social media content creation will be completed independently and asynchronously. Event support is provided in real time during live Zoom sessions, which may include nights and/or weekends. A schedule of upcoming events will be provided well in advance, and the supervisor will work with the student to confirm availability and coverage. Skills You’ll Gain Develop hands-on experience in social media content creation and digital communications Grow professional communication skills for online and live event settings Build event coordination skills, including hosting, chat moderation, and technical troubleshooting on Zoom Strengthen confidence in public speaking through introducing presenters and engaging with event attendees Practice working independently while collaborating with a professional team Qualifications Must be detail oriented, professional, comfortable with technology, and facile in the use of social media in professional settings. This position entails the creation of friendly, upbeat copy as well the capacity to learn about the various hashtags and sources used in the field. Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Email a CV or resume to Laura Thomas Email: Email a CV or resume to Laura Thomas Position Type: Work Study Department: Education To apply for this job please visit Email%20a%20CV%20or%20resume%20to%20Laura%20Thomas . Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.antioch.edu/job/data-analyst-assistant-a-erdynast-work-study/": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Research Assistant - Data Analyst - A. Erdynast [Work Study] - Antioch University Skip to content Give Now Request Info Visit Apply Employment About About About Antioch University Our Schools Core Attributes of an Antioch Education Why Antioch University? Office for Inclusive Excellence & Student Affairs (OIESA) Antioch Forward History Common Thread Leadership Office of the President Executive Leadership Board of Governors Administrative Resources Accreditation University Policies Discover Our Campuses Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Academics Discover Your Own Path Explore degrees that align with your passions and goals. Find your fit today and take the first step toward a meaningful future. Find Your Program Academic Focus Areas Bachelor's Completion Creative Writing Counseling, Psychology, & Therapy Education Environmental Studies & Sustainability Individualized Studies Leadership & Management Nursing & Health Professions Learn Your Way Low-Residency On-Campus Online Programs by Type Doctoral Master's Bachelor's Certificates Credentials & Endorsements Continuing Education Admission & Aid Admissions Admissions Overview Unofficial Transcript Evaluation Upcoming Admissions Events What to Expect Information for DREAMERS International Students Transfer & Degree Completion Students Veterans & Military-Connected Students Dates & Deadlines Graduate School of Leadership & Change Los Angeles New England Online Santa Barbara Seattle Tuition & Fees GSLC Tuition & Fees AULA Tuition & Fees AUNE Tuition & Fees AUO Tuition & Fees AUSB Tuition & Fees AUS Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Financial Aid Overview Financial Aid Forms Scholarships & Grants Types of Aid Work-Study Opportunities Library WorldCat Library Catalog Wherever you are in your research journey, the Antioch University librarians can help you find what you need. One of the major library tools to know about is WorldCat, the world’s largest library catalog. The catalog connects you with resources in the Antioch University Library and other libraries worldwide. Explore the Catalog Library Getting Started A-Z Resources Research Guides Dissertation HQ Borrow and Request Help Information For Alumni Visitors and Libraries About Locations Hours Directory Policies Resources Departments & Offices Advancement Disability Support Services Grants and Foundation Relations Information Technology Institutional Effectiveness Registrar Strategic Partnerships Student Accounts Writing Support Academic Resources Academic Assessment Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Bookstore Consumer Information Licensure Information Resource List Student Policies University Policies Additional Resources President's Communications Event Calendar Common Thread (University News) Alumni Magazine Faculty Directory Report/Request It Hub Home » Work at Antioch › Research Assistant - Data Analyst - A. Erdynast [Work Study] Research Assistant - Data Analyst - A. Erdynast [Work Study] Work-Study (AULA) Remote (Remote) Posted 6 months ago Antioch Unviversity Los Angeles Start Date: 7/1/2026 End Date: 6/30/2027 Number of Positions: 4 1 Assistant operates Zoom sessions in two classes per quarter. One Assistnt works on case studies including case studies on Harold Pinter, Vivien Merchant and Antonia Fraser and Hollywood celebrities. One assistant works on data analysis of questionnaires on three types of generosity and two types of compassion. One Assistant works on data analysis of conceptions of the good and terms of right and strains of commitment in Hollywood marriages and divorces. Hours per Week: 20 hrs/wk Weekends Required: No Evenings Required: Yes Supervisor: Albert Erdynast Alternate Supervisor: Kathryn Pope This position allows for remote work Yes/No: Yes Percentage of time that could be remote (0-100%): 100% Method to assess remote work: Specific assignments and time will be estimated for the tasks to be completed Job Description Student provides assistance to Dr. Albert Erdynast. Specific duties include technical support: running Zoom for Dr. Erdynast’s classes, screenshare, creation of breakout rooms, playing films for class. Also, updating syllabi and Sakai pages for classes, providing general student support, editing academic papers. Available to edit multiple manuscripts in psychology. Enter data in Excel for research projects. Student should be skilled on APA Style 7 and familiar with Excel. Antioch University provides equal opportunity for all qualified applicants and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected classification. Qualifications Antioch BA or MAP student Does this position meet the definition of Community Service? No How to Apply: Apply to Albert Erdynast. Resume document Email: [email protected] Position Type: Work Study Department: SIPS To apply for this job email your details to aerdynast@antioch.edu Back to Job Listings Search CA Disclosures Privacy Policy Resources Terms & Conditions Contact Antioch University is a proud co-founder of the Coalition for the Common Good © Antioch University 2026. All rights reserved."
    },
